{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1510839540,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzQ1MTg3MzU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1971","origin":"github"},"title":"metadata-aggregation fails to rewrite an unavailable object file","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nA dataset was clone. The actual data content was made available locally, but none of the aggregated metadata objects that were annex'ed due to their size are available locally. Re-aggregation in this situation computes the exact same information and wants to write it in the a file of the same name as before (all correct). But this happens:\n\n```\n[ERROR  ] [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../.datalad/metadata/objects/bd/cn-dc6cf454dd1fa41257afb374ef6666' [json_py.py:dump2xzstream:67] (IOError) \n```\n\nBecause the existing link does not point to an actual file.\n\nIn this case even `unlock()` is not the right thing to do, but we should rather `git rm` the file without a commit, before rewriting them, maybe.","files":null}]}